# Assignment 4 – Repository with at Least Three Meaningful Commits

## 1. Objective

The objective of this assignment is to understand Git version control, initialize a repository, track changes, and create at least three meaningful commits.

## 2. Git Identity Configuration

Commands used to configure Git identity:

```bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"
```

## 3. Repository Initialization

```bash
git init
git branch -M main
```

## 4. Meaningful Commits

I created the following three commits:

| Commit No. | Commit Message             |
| ---------- | -------------------------- |
| 1          | Initial commit             |
| 2          | Add new file index.html    |
| 3          | docs: add learning journey |

5. Git Commands Used

bash
git status
git add README.md
git commit -m "docs: add learning journey"
git log --oneline
git push origin main


 6. Commit History

The following command was used to check the commit history:

bash
git log --oneline


 7. Conclusion

I successfully learned how to configure Git, initialize a repository, track file changes, create meaningful commits, and view commit history. I also learned how to upload my local repository changes to GitHub.
